<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Jaxartes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">329 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great">Wars of Alexander the Great</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Jaxartes was fought in 329 BCE on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>, near the newly founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria-eschate">Alexandria Eschate</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and Saka nomads from beyond the river. Using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catapult">catapults</a> to cover the crossing and combining cavalry with light troops to pin the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mounted-archer">mounted archers</a>, Alexander won a clear victory. He then made peace with the Saka rather than pursue them into the steppe.</p></div>
